HHIISSTTOORRYY
       The ccoonnsstt modifiers were added to the structure pointer arguments of
       ooppeennppttyy() and ffoorrkkppttyy() in glibc 2.8.

       Before glibc 2.0.92, ooppeennppttyy() returns file descriptors for a BSD
       pseudoterminal pair; since glibc 2.0.92, it first attempts to open a
       UNIX 98 pseudoterminal pair, and falls back to opening a BSD
       pseudoterminal pair if that fails.

BBUUGGSS
       Nobody knows how much space should be reserved for _n_a_m_e.  So, calling
       ooppeennppttyy() or ffoorrkkppttyy() with non‐NULL _n_a_m_e may not be secure.

